\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


Write $\mathbb D=\{z\in\mathbb C:|z|<1\}$ and $\mathbb T=\partial\mathbb D$. Let $S$ consist of holomorphic injective functions $f(z)=z+\sum_{n\ge2}a_nz^n$ on $\mathbb D$; set $a_0=0$, $a_1=1$. A function in $S$ is starlike if its image is starlike about $0$, and convex if its image is a convex domain.Suppose for constants $\lambda\in\mathbb C\setminus\{0\}$ and $\delta>0$ that $(1-r)^2f(r)=\lambda+O((1-r)^\delta)$ as real $r\uparrow1$. The constants in all asymptotics may depend on $f,\lambda,\delta$.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Determine the sharp improvement, under exactly this hypothesis, of the estimate $a_n/n=\lambda+O(1/\log n)$ as $n\to\infty$. \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07200}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
How quickly must the normalized coefficients approach the nonzero radial growth limit when the radial error has a positive power rate?

